{"id":"adf0514792f601bda63f236476712eacc4554bfd","axis":"silent","repo":"microsoft/playwright","sha":"adf0514792f601bda63f236476712eacc4554bfd","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/src/test-reporters-js.md","lines":["@@ -79,6 +79,25 @@ export default defineConfig({"," });"," ```"," ","+### Redacting secrets","+","+Pass a `secrets` list to any reporter, built-in or custom, to hide sensitive values in its output. Each entry has a `value` with the sensitive text, and an optional `name`. The reporter sees `<secret>NAME</secret>`, or `<secret/>` for an entry without a name, in place of the value in test and step titles, errors, console output, attachment names and attachment bodies.","+","+```js title=\"playwright.config.ts\"","+import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';","+","+export default defineConfig({","+  reporter: [","+    ['list'],","+    ['html', { secrets: [{ name: 'PASSWORD', value: process.env.PASSWORD }] }],","+  ],","+});","+```","+","+In this example, the terminal output is not changed, while the HTML report never contains the password.","+","+Values are matched as plain text, so a short value could match unrelated text. Screenshots, videos, trace files, and attachments referenced by path are not changed.","+"," ## Built-in reporters"," "," All built-in reporters show detailed information about failures, and mostly differ in verbosity for successful runs."],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/isomorphic/index.ts","lines":["@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@ export * from './multimap';"," export * from './protocolFormatter';"," export * from './protocolMetainfo';"," export * from './rtti';","+export * from './secrets';"," export * from './semaphore';"," export * from './stringUtils';"," export * from './formatUtils';"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/isomorphic/secrets.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@","+/**","+ * Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.","+ *","+ * Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");","+ * you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.","+ * You may obtain a copy of the License at","+ *","+ * http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+ *","+ * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software","+ * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,","+ * WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.","+ * See the License for the specific language governing permissions and","+ * limitations under the License.","+ */","+","+export type Secrets = { name?: string, value: string }[];","+","+// Longer values go first, so that a secret that contains another secret is replaced as a whole.","+export function normalizeSecrets(secrets: Secrets | undefined): Secrets {","+  if (!secrets)","+    return [];","+  return secrets","+      .filter(secret => typeof secret?.value === 'string' && secret.value.length > 0)","+      .sort((a, b) => b.value.length - a.value.length);","+}","+","+export function secretsKey(secrets: Secrets | undefined): string {","+  return JSON.stringify(normalizeSecrets(secrets).map(secret => JSON.stringify([secret.name ?? null, secret.value])).sort());","+}","+","+export function secretPlaceholder(name: string | undefined): string {","+  return name ? `<secret>${name}</secret>` : `<secret/>`;","+}","+","+export function redactSecrets(text: string, secrets: Secrets): string {","+  for (const { name, value } of secrets)","+    text = text.replaceAll(value, secretPlaceholder(name));","+  return text;","+}","+","+export function redactSecretsInJSON(json: string, secrets: Secrets): string {","+  for (const { name, value } of secrets) {","+    const escapedValue = JSON.stringify(value).slice(1, -1);","+    const escapedPlaceholder = JSON.stringify(secretPlaceholder(name)).slice(1, -1);","+    json = json.replaceAll(escapedValue, escapedPlaceholder);","+  }","+  return json;","+}","+","+// The buffer is not decoded, because it may not be a valid utf-8 string.","+export function redactSecretsInBuffer(buffer: Buffer, secrets: Secrets): Buffer {","+  for (const { name, value } of secrets) {","+    const needle = Buffer.from(value, 'utf8');","+    let index = buffer.indexOf(needle);","+    if (index === -1)","+      continue;","+    const replacement = Buffer.from(secretPlaceholder(name), 'utf8');","+    const chunks: Buffer[] = [];","+    let start = 0;","+    while (index !== -1) {","+      chunks.push(buffer.subarray(start, index), replacement);","+      start = index + needle.length;","+      index = buffer.indexOf(needle, start);","+    }","+    chunks.push(buffer.subarray(start));","+    buffer = Buffer.concat(chunks);","+  }","+  return buffer;","+}"],"additions":70,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/playwright/src/cli/reportActions.ts","lines":["@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ export async function mergeReports(reportDir: string | undefined, opts: { [key:","     throw new Error(`\"${dir}\" is not a directory`);","   let reporterDescriptions: ReporterDescription[] | undefined = resolveReporterOption(opts.reporter);","   if (!reporterDescriptions && configFile)","-    reporterDescriptions = config.config.reporter;","+    reporterDescriptions = config.reporterDescriptions;","   if (!reporterDescriptions)","     reporterDescriptions = [[commonConfig.defaultReporter]];","   const rootDirOverride = configFile ? config.config.rootDir : undefined;"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/playwright/src/common/config.ts","lines":["@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ export class FullConfigInternal {","   readonly singleTSConfigPath?: string;","   readonly captureGitInfo: Config['captureGitInfo'];","   readonly retryStrategy: 'immediate' | 'isolated';","+  readonly reporterDescriptions: ReporterDescription[];  // Includes secrets, unlike FullConfig.reporter","   defineConfigWasUsed = false;"," ","   globalSetups: string[] = [];","@@ -77,6 +78,8 @@ export class FullConfigInternal {","     // so that plu